  "title": "Celtics Land Fournier For Two Second Round Picks",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":510834,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/GettyImages-1124297303-1024x721.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-510834\"/><figcaption>NEW YORK, NEW YORK - JANUARY 23:  Evan Fournier #10<span style=\"font-size:0px; color:#ff0000;\">﻿\n</span> of the Orlando Magic drives against D'Angelo Russell #1 of the Brooklyn Nets during their game at the Barclays Center on January 23, 2019 in New York City.  NOTE TO USER: User expressly acknowledges and agrees that, by downloading and or using this photograph, User is consenting to the terms and conditions of the Getty Images License Agreement. (Photo by Al Bello/Getty Images)</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>According to ESPN's Adrian Wojnarowski, the Boston Celtics are finalizing an agreement to acquire Orlando Magic  Evan Fournier for two second-round picks ahead of Thursday's tra<span style=\"font-size:0px; color:#ff0000;\">﻿\n</span>de deadline.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/wojespn/status/1375107558709542921?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/wojespn/status/1375107558709542921?s=20\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>After <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/30826587/with-superstars-market-2021-nba-trade-deadline-quiet\">ESPN's Tim Bontemps </a>reported in February, Fournier was \"expected to attract interest\" due to his expiring contract. It makes sense for the Magic to move it since it is intended to strike free agency after the 2020-21 season.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>After all, Orlando is no realistic title contender and has been able to save something back for the player before he potentially leaves to join another team.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Fournier averages 19.7 points out of 46.1% shots, 3.7 assists, and 2.9 rebounds per night this season as a person who can attack the defense from the bounce defends several positions, and hit from the outside, as evidenced by its 39.9 percent long-range music video last season.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
